From 78f19f4ab1b66871b60f2e1144920e0844b6bc45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:31:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Viewer track: stage joints ("sp")

Each stage part with a joint tree in the stage's file writes its joints as
its animations and code left them at the frame's end, delta-coded like "jp":
a joint is written once it leaves the file's rest pose, then on change. The
part is numbered as "gjoint" numbers it, the joint by preorder index as
stage_joint counts it (0 the part's scale root from Ground_801C14D0). The
pose owners and the line buffer grow to fit a stage part's tree. Unlocked
until a recording is compared against the game's stage poses.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017JX71xgnBPBiwucag1mFRr
---
 agent_docs/VIEWER_TRACK.md       |   3 +
 src/runtime/viewer_track.c       | 136 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 tools/validation/visual_state.py |   1 +
 3 files changed, 126 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

